<p>In the latest sign of the widening Middle East war, Yemen&#x27;s Houthi movement said it carried out a second attack on Israel in less than 24 hours, using missiles and drones, after launching its first such strike since the Iran war began. Israel&#x27;s military said it intercepted at least one missile fired from Yemen and reported no injuries from the initial attack, but the Houthis&#x27; renewed involvement has raised concern that the conflict could spread further across the region. The escalation comes as the war enters its second month and the United States sends additional forces into the region, including about 3,500 more troops and arriving Marines, while Washington waits for Tehran&#x27;s formal response to a 15-point peace proposal. Several reports also said Iran signaled that ships from what it called &quot;nonhostile&quot; nations could pass through the Strait of Hormuz, a limited sign that some maritime traffic might continue even as shipping and regional security remain under heavy strain.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zUN2wUopcp6p-3oKnL66MsWPSu2f95IDq917DngqGqk1tLPkv66dkVZ-I-Amlq0kM47dDwWpUNuekoRdLuimMqgt_-NtO6WmjqdwrfQJym3tJT6rqoywGN-ioj0FRiNlfMmzsJaxSLFMzwRYmKOpwocYJ_7P0uxTkecXUmIg0wE3D_EfWblYmb_GWsSBvb05gy7-d5R9ywOmQv4xKqX2sytE' alt='Houthi supporters in Sanaa, Yemen, demonstrating in solidarity with Iran on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>US casualties: A U.S. official told The New York Times that an earlier Iranian strike on a military base in Saudi Arabia injured around two dozen U.S. troops, while NPR reported that at least 15 U.S. personnel were wounded.</li><li>Medical strain: Dawn reported that Israel had recorded 5,689 wartime injuries, putting hospitals under pressure as the fighting widened.</li><li>Diplomatic effort: Pakistan said it would host talks on Monday with the foreign ministers of Saudi Arabia, Turkey, and Egypt to seek a regional approach to ending the conflict.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Houthi movement: The group said it was entering the war in support of Iran and other &quot;resistance&quot; factions and vowed to keep attacking until what it called aggression on all fronts ends. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/29/as-war-on-iran-enters-second-month-yemens-houthis-open-new-front'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Israeli military: Israeli forces said they intercepted missiles launched from Yemen and are preparing for what a military spokesperson described as a multifront war. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/yemens-houthis-claim-first-missile-attack-on-israel-since-war-began'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>United States: Secretary of State Marco Rubio said before the strike that the United States expected to conclude military operations within weeks, even as more U.S. forces arrived in the region. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/yemens-houthis-strike-israel-their-first-such-attack-iran-war-began'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iran: Tehran said ships from &quot;nonhostile&quot; nations could pass through the Strait of Hormuz, signaling that it was drawing distinctions among countries even as pressure on maritime traffic mounted. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/houthi-iran-israel-war-hormuz-pakistan-shipping/33718789.html'>Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-houthis-claim-2nd-attack-on-israel-in-24-hours/live-76573681'>Iran war: Houthis claim 2nd attack on Israel in 24 hours</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/29/as-war-on-iran-enters-second-month-yemens-houthis-open-new-front'>As war on Iran enters second month, Yemen’s Houthis open new front</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/houthi-iran-israel-war-hormuz-pakistan-shipping/33718789.html'>Houthis Strike Israel Again, While Iran To Allow &#x27;Nonhostile&#x27; Nations&#x27; Ships Through Strait</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.al